1
00:00:03,109 --> 00:00:05,983
Mila catches a snowflake on her mitten:

2
00:00:06,033 --> 00:00:08,308
a tiny star, with six branches.

3
00:00:08,358 --> 00:00:09,582
Then another one…

4
00:00:09,632 --> 00:00:12,057
six too, never five, never seven!

5
00:00:12,107 --> 00:00:12,707
Why six?

6
00:00:13,490 --> 00:00:16,658
Under the magnifying glass, every snowflake is different,

7
00:00:16,708 --> 00:00:18,126
but all have six branches.

8
00:00:18,176 --> 00:00:21,394
So Noah's drawing, with too many branches, is impossible!

9
00:00:22,182 --> 00:00:23,696
Discovery mission!

10
00:00:26,212 --> 00:00:26,870
Mini mode!

11
00:00:26,920 --> 00:00:28,003
In an icy cloud,

12
00:00:28,053 --> 00:00:31,473
a very cold droplet freezes onto a speck of dust.

13
00:00:31,523 --> 00:00:33,669
Then water vapor turns straight

14
00:00:33,719 --> 00:00:35,347
into ice all around it.

15
00:00:36,138 --> 00:00:39,723
When freezing, water molecules always line up the same way:

16
00:00:39,773 --> 00:00:41,448
in hexagons, with six sides.

17
00:00:41,498 --> 00:00:43,666
So the crystal grows with six sides,

18
00:00:43,716 --> 00:00:44,825
then six branches.

19
00:00:45,601 --> 00:00:49,952
As it falls, the snowflake travels through air that is more or less cold and humid,

20
00:00:50,002 --> 00:00:51,702
so its branches grow differently.

21
00:00:51,752 --> 00:00:53,717
But since all six live the same story,

22
00:00:53,767 --> 00:00:54,616
they stay alike.

23
00:00:55,422 --> 00:00:58,439
And since no two snowflakes make exactly the same journey,

24
00:00:58,489 --> 00:00:59,338
no two are alike…

25
00:00:59,388 --> 00:01:02,085
billions of six-branched stars fall, all different!

26
00:01:02,880 --> 00:01:05,277
And that's why snowflakes have six branches.

27
00:01:06,439 --> 00:01:08,183
Ice builds itself in hexagons;

28
00:01:08,233 --> 00:01:10,806
so every snowflake grows with six branches.

29
00:01:11,591 --> 00:01:15,148
With an adult, on a snowy day: catch snowflakes on a dark glove,

30
00:01:15,198 --> 00:01:17,234
look at them with a magnifying glass…

31
00:01:17,284 --> 00:01:18,580
and count the branches!

32
00:01:19,371 --> 00:01:21,313
And why do the seasons change?

33
00:01:21,363 --> 00:01:22,691
The answer tomorrow.
